the technique of debate is a really  interesting and useful technique I make  sure to arbitrarily assign students the  side that they'll be taking in the  debate because it's pretty easy to  debate something that you feel  passionate about it's not so easy to  debate something that you don't feel  passionate about or where you feel the  other side is correct in terms of  learning it really is a I think it's a  great exercise because it forces people  to at least superficially understand the  stated arguments for the side they're  taking and then find a way to at least  be semi convincing about those arguments  and then I give them a period of time to  prepare to sort of prepare their  arguments about how they're going to  defend their positions and and then I  have them voice voice their arguments  for the particular side that they've  been assigned  so in crafting the arguments Pro if  you're a con you really have to start to  understand what goes behind those  arguments a little bit better and so  that's where the learning takes place I  think the other thing is that the  students get a little bit competitive so  they want to construct a good argument  they want to sound convincing and so  that extra little bit means that they  really do put in the effort to construct  a good argument and to make it  believable if I were making  recommendations to someone who had never  used a debate before I would say that  you should first of all don't pick  anything that's really emotional to  start out with so people can fiat have a  pretty strong opinion about it but it's  not something that's really deep so I  would stay away from something too too  touchy the other thing is there should  be it should be something where it's  really not a slam dunk one way or the  other so you want to make sure that the  the the topic that you choose really  does have two reasonable positions you  don't want to give one team just a  terrible thing to have to argue the  other thing you want to make sure is  that you give students enough time to  craft their arguments and to to debate  to debate the points so if you cut the  debate short after three minutes it's  just not going to help so you have to  set aside a pretty good chunk of time
 

